1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,140
每时每刻我们都能感受到它，
We feel it every moment of our lives.

2
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:09,810
但对物理学家来说...
But for physicists...

3
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:15,130
这是宇宙最古老的谜团，
It is the oldest unsolved mystery of the cosmos.

4
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:18,010
为什么引力使得物体之间相互吸引？
Why does gravity make everything attract?

5
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:27,860
最前沿的理论带给我们了意外的答案，
Cutting-edge theory is closing in on unexpected answers.

6
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:32,560
引力是否是另一种力的表现形式...
Could gravity be another force in disguise...

7
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,130
一个全息现实的影子，
A shadow of a holographic reality,

8
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:41,700
或是虚幻的涟漪？
or a rippling mirage?

9
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:46,310
我们，地球，太阳和其他恒星
Do we, Earth, the Sun, and the stars

10
00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:48,940
真的有重量吗？
really have weight?

11
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:53,110
难道引力只是一个幻觉？
Or is gravity an illusion?

12
00:00:56,720 --> 00:01:01,760
空间，时间，生命本身。
Space, time, life itself.

13
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:08,860
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:19,190
引力真的存在吗？

15
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,980
太阳的引力使地球
The gravitational pull of the sun

16
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:29,080
围绕太阳运行而不会脱离轨道。
keeps Earth from flying off into space.

17
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,320
地球的引力使我们牢牢地站在地面上，
Earth's gravity keeps us firmly planted on the ground.

18
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:36,190
这一切都看起来那么真实。
This all seems real enough.

19
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:40,730
科学家们则深入到宇宙的结构之中，
But scientists are peering deep into the fabric of the universe

20
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:44,830
发现引力...
and are discovering that gravity...

21
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:50,700
...也许并不是它看起来的这样。
...may not be what it seems to be.

22
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:56,640
我们觉得真实的东西会是虚幻的吗？
Can something feel real but not actually be real?

23
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:02,710
在我成长的日子里，
There were some days growing up

24
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:05,780
有些时候没什么事可做，
when there just wasn't anything to do.

25
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:08,800
我们就会玩一些简单的游戏，
So we would play simple games

26
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:11,520
比如扔石头。
like target practice with rocks.

27
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:16,660
引力一直发挥着作用，
Gravity always worked.

28
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:21,400
无论我扔出什么东西，它都会掉在地上。
No matter what I dropped, I always expected it to fall.

29
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:33,110
物理学家对引力有着自己的见解，
Physicists have their own expectations about gravity.

30
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:35,050
他们认为引力是一种基本力，
They believe it to be a fundamental force,

31
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:39,450
是宇宙的基本组成结构。
an intrinsic cog in the machinery of the universe.

32
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:43,520
但实验物理学家Nergis Mavalvala
But experimentalist Nergis Mavalvala

33
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,090
并不认为这一切都是理所当然的。
isn't taking anything for granted.

34
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:51,230
一种基本力--比如引力，
So, a fundamental force that -- like gravity,

35
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:55,200
用来描述有质量物体间的相互作用，
that describes how massive objects interact

36
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,370
我们认为引力是真实存在的。
should be true anywhere you look in the universe.

37
00:02:58,370 --> 00:03:03,010
艾萨克·牛顿发现任何有质量的物体
Isaac Newton showed that every object with mass

38
00:03:03,010 --> 00:03:05,940
都会互相吸引。
attracts every other object with mass.

39
00:03:05,950 --> 00:03:08,650
两个物体质量越大，距离越小，
The greater the mass and the closer they are,

40
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:12,080
它们之间的万有引力就越大。
the greater the gravitational attraction.

41
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:14,150
两百多年后，
Over 200 years later,

42
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:18,220
阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦解释了为什么会这样，
Albert Einstein explained why this happens.

43
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:23,760
空间和时间互相交织形成时空，
Space and time are interwoven into a fabric called spacetime.

44
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:29,900
爱因斯坦认为时空可以弯曲，
Einstein believed that spacetime could bend.

45
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:34,410
这种时空形变产生了引力，
This distortion is what we experience as gravity.

46
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:37,570
这是他如何理解有质量物体间的
And that's how he understood that objects with mass

47
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:38,990
相互吸引，
attract to each other.

48
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:41,510
物体随时空弯曲运动，
They follow the curvature of spacetime.

49
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:44,210
爱因斯坦对引力的描述
So Einstein's picture of -- of gravity was

50
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,930
表明质量是时空扭曲的表现，
that mass tells spacetime how to curve,

51
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,490
时空的扭曲，
and then the curvature of spacetime

52
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:51,650
告诉物体如何运动。
tells mass how to move.

53
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:55,060
爱因斯坦也预测了
Einstein also predicted

54
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:58,060
当有质量的物体运动时，
that when all objects with mass move,

55
00:03:58,060 --> 00:04:01,030
会引起时空结构中
they trigger tiny gravitational ripples

56
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:03,030
微弱的引力波动。
in the fabric of spacetime.

57
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:07,740
引力波会波及我们头上的天空。
Gravitational waves should permeate the heavens above us.

58
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:11,670
Nergis认为如果这些波足够大，
Nergis believes we should be able to detect those waves,

59
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:14,080
我们就能够检测到它们。
if they are big enough.

60
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:19,280
如果我往池塘中间扔出一个苹果...
So if I drop an apple in the middle of a pond...

61
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:23,190
我在岸边检测水波强度，
And I try to detect the ripple at the shore,

62
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:24,790
这基本是不可能的，
it's not going to make it.

63
00:04:24,790 --> 00:04:27,060
这个波过于微弱了。
It was too small of a wave.

64
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,970
对Nergis来说，幸运的是
Luckily for Nergis,

65
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:31,660
天空中引起波动的物体
bodies much more massive than apples

66
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:33,530
比苹果大得多。
cause a stir in the heavens.

67
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,940
牛逼！哇哦！
Awesome! Whoa!

68
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:48,010
整个宇宙中，
Around the cosmos,

69
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:50,000
剧烈的引力事件，
intense gravitational events,

70
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,350
比如星系之间的碰撞...
like the collision of galaxies...

71
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:58,020
...或是巨星的爆发...
...or the explosions of giant stars...

72
00:04:59,290 --> 00:05:01,220
...都会向着地球发出
...should be sending massive volleys

73
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:05,580
引力波信号。
of gravitational waves towards Earth.

74
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:08,230
Nergis发明了一种检测它们的方法，
Nergis has created a way to detect them

75
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:12,230
这需要像Mike Landry这样的同事的帮助。
with the help of collaborators like Mike Landry.

76
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,450
Nergis和Mike
Nergis and Mike

77
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:17,570
是美国国家科学基金会建造的
are part of the largest experiment ever built

78
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:20,370
最大的实验室成员之一。
by the National Science Foundation.

79
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:21,710
它就是
It is known as

80
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:24,750
激光干涉引力波天文台，
the Laser Interferometer Gravitational Wave observatory,

81
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,510
简称为L.I.G.O.，
or L.I.G.O.,

82
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,300
在这个庞然大物中，
in this behemoth,

83
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:31,620
激光束射向两个
laser beams fire down two vacuum tubes

84
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,320
以L型排布的真空管，
arranged in an "L" shape.

85
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:39,410
每个臂都有4公里长。
Each arm is 4 kilometers long.

86
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:41,930
激光束在每个臂中测量扰动的精度
The laser beams can measure the length of each arm

87
00:05:41,930 --> 00:05:44,580
可以达到一个原子宽度的
with an accuracy of better than 1 millionth

88
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:46,100
一百万分之一。
of the width of an atom.

89
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:51,140
如果距离我们有500兆兆英里远的
If a gravitational wave from any intense cosmic event

90
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:54,340
某个剧烈宇宙事件产生了引力波
up to 500 trillion trillion miles away

91
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:56,110
经过了地球，
passes through the Earth,

92
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:58,710
管子中的空间就会波动，
the space inside the tubes will ripple.

93
00:05:58,710 --> 00:06:01,010
激光束就可以检测到变化，
The lasers will detect the change,

94
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:03,520
提示铃就会响。
and the alarm bells will ring.

95
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:12,110
对天空将近十年的聆听，
After almost a decade of listening to the heavens,

96
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:14,090
L.I.G.O.没有检测到...
L.I.G.O. picked up the sound...

97
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:16,550
...任何明显信号。
...of crickets.

98
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,680
在L.I.G.O.运行初期
We didn't observe a gravitational wave

99
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:23,500
我们并没有观察到引力波。
in the initial science runs of L.I.G.O.

100
00:06:24,210 --> 00:06:27,210
Nergis, Mike和L.I.G.O.的数千位科学家
Nergis, Mike, and the thousands of scientists at L.I.G.O.

101
00:06:27,210 --> 00:06:28,870
还有一招，
Have one more shot.

102
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:32,010
他们正尝试使用先进的设备
They're working on advanced upgrades

103
00:06:32,010 --> 00:06:35,510
来使L.I.G.O.的检测敏感程度增加十倍，
that will increase L.I.G.O.'s sensitivity tenfold.

104
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:39,280
但这仍不能保证他们就能够获得引力波信号。
But there's no guarantee they'll ever get a signal.

105
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:41,950
如果使用如此先进的L.I.G.O.
Well, if we don't detect gravitational waves

106
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,690
还检测不到引力波的话，我就要哭了，
with advanced L.I.G.O., well, first, I'll cry.

107
00:06:44,690 --> 00:06:47,880
但之后我觉得现在的结果同样令人兴奋，
But then, I think, it's actually very exciting either way.

108
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,030
如果我们检测不到引力波，
If we don't see gravitational waves,

109
00:06:50,030 --> 00:06:53,500
那么一场新的革命就会开始，
then it's going to start off a different kind of revolution,

110
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,100
人们就会努力去思考
where there'll be a lot of head-scratching

111
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:59,140
“到底大自然还有什么是我们不了解的？”
about, "what is it about nature we don't understand?"

112
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:03,060
Nergis对此充满希望。
Nergis is hopeful.

113
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:07,380
事实上，2014年三月，一组宇航员
In fact, in march of 2014, a group of astronomers

114
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:10,280
声称他们检测到了
claimed to have detected gravitational waves

115
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,920
由大爆炸产生的引力波。
produced by the big bang.

116
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:14,320
而一些科学家认为
But some scientists take

117
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,770
L.I.G.O.并未监测到任何信号
the deafening silence at L.I.G.O.

118
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:20,290
恰好说明引力也许并不是基本力，
as evidence that gravity may not be a fundamental force.

119
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:23,290
苹果成熟后向地面掉落，
When an apple falls to the earth,

120
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:26,660
也许是其他原因造成的。
something else could be pulling it down.

121
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:29,950
物理学家们认为宇宙万物，
Physicists believe that everything in the universe,

122
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:33,440
包括一股我们称作力的能量，
even the pulse of energy that we call force,

123
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:36,270
都是由粒子构成的，
is made from particles.

124
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:39,610
引力也不例外。
Gravity should be no exception.

125
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:54,370
Zvi Bern是一位粒子物理学家，
Zvi Bern is a particle physicist

126
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:57,560
他有着非常丰富的想象力。
with a very active imagination.

127
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:02,320
他正在设想如果把高尔夫球
He's imagining what a game of mini golf would look like

128
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,980
压缩到亚原子粒子的大小、
if the balls were shrunk

129
00:08:03,990 --> 00:08:06,640
并遵循量子力学规律后，
to the size of subatomic particles

130
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:10,510
应该如何玩这场迷你高尔夫球呢？
and ruled by the laws of quantum mechanics.

131
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:14,380
量子力学中充斥着你能想象到的
Quantum mechanics is full of the strangest things

132
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:16,530
各种奇怪的事。
you can imagine.

133
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:19,500
一个粒子所处的位置的概念
The concept of a particle being at one point,

134
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:22,850
在量子力学中变得非常模糊。
that becomes a very fuzzy concept in quantum mechanics.

135
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:27,660
亚原子粒子不同于任何
Subatomic particles are unlike anything

136
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:29,810
你肉眼可以看到的物体，
you can see with your naked eye.

137
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:33,230
如果没人观察，它们会变得非常模糊，
They become fuzzy when no one looks at them.

138
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:37,670
它们有时会无中生有...
Sometimes they can appear out of nowhere...

139
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:40,470
然后又突然消失。
and then suddenly vanish.

140
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:43,040
这些出现又消失的粒子...
Some of these appearing and disappearing particles...

141
00:08:44,310 --> 00:08:47,180
...传递着基本自然力--
...transmit the fundamental forces of nature --

142
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:50,750
电磁力、强力、
electromagnetism, the strong force,

143
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:55,970
弱力，和可能存在的引力。
the weak force, and, supposedly, gravity.

144
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:57,890
我有一个高尔夫球，
I have here a golf ball.

145
00:08:57,890 --> 00:09:00,520
假设它代表了一个光子，
The golf ball represents a photon.

146
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:04,190
光子是电磁力的载体，
The photon is the carrier of the electromagnetic force.

147
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:08,730
通过电荷，电磁力使物质
The electromagnetic force attracts or repels

148
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:11,570
互相吸引或排斥，
anything with an electric charge.

149
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:12,930
另有一些高尔夫球--
The next golf balls --

150
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,170
代表W和Z波色子，
these represent the W and the Z boson.

151
00:09:15,170 --> 00:09:16,460
W和Z波色子--
The W and the Z boson --

152
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:19,470
是弱相互作用的载体，
these are the carriers of the weak nuclear interaction.

153
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,780
弱力使得
The weak force causes

154
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:22,510
放射性原子的原子核
the nucleus of a radioactive atom

155
00:09:22,510 --> 00:09:24,080
发生破碎。
to break apart.

156
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:27,050
接下来的高尔夫球，代表了胶子，
The next golf ball -- it represents the gluon.

157
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:30,050
胶子是强相互作用的载体，
The gluon is the carrier of the strong nuclear interaction.

158
00:09:30,050 --> 00:09:33,390
强力使得粒子组合在一起，
The strong force binds particles together

159
00:09:33,390 --> 00:09:37,430
形成原子核。
to form an atomic nucleus.

160
00:09:37,430 --> 00:09:40,800
引力也应该由一种粒子所承载，
Gravity should also be carried by a particle,

161
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:45,730
但还没有人发现所谓的引力子，
but no one has ever observed this so-called graviton.

162
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:50,840
事实上，当物理学家尝试计算
In fact, when physicists try to calculate

163
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,940
引力子理论上如何运作时，
how the theoretical graviton might work,

164
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:57,110
他们很快就陷入了数学困境之中。
they quickly get lost in impossible math.

165
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:59,650
不幸的是，引力是这些计算中
Gravity, unfortunately, is one of our most complicated theories

166
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:01,280
最为复杂的理论之一，
in the way it interacts.

167
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:04,780
原因是当你在做这些计算时，
And what happens is as you do these calculations,

168
00:10:04,790 --> 00:10:07,140
很快就会遇到一些公式，
very quickly you start encountering expressions

169
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:08,690
这个世界上还没有计算机，
which no computer in the world,

170
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,440
或者说所有的计算机--
or all the world's computer --

171
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,160
都不能满足计算的需要。
they couldn't possibly do those calculations.

172
00:10:14,730 --> 00:10:17,100
但Zvi还有一个办法
But Zvi has a trick up his sleeve

173
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:21,000
能够计算引力子是否存在。
to calculate whether or not the graviton exists.

174
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:26,170
量子理论，就像迷你高尔夫一样，是一个概率的游戏，
Quantum theory, like mini golf, is a game of probability.

175
00:10:26,170 --> 00:10:30,040
一杆进洞是非常困难的，
Trying to hit a hole-in-one is difficult.

176
00:10:30,050 --> 00:10:32,780
高尔夫球有很多种运行方式，
